# Profile stack: nested push pattern

When pushing a screen **from a view that was itself pushed** onto Profile’s `NavigationStack` (e.g. Edit Profile → Wardrobe Privacy, Friends → other-user profile):

## Do

- Use **`navigationDestination(item:)`** with an optional `Identifiable` / `Hashable` destination value.
- Set the value from a `Button` (or equivalent); keep the destination on the **parent Profile stack** — no nested `NavigationStack`.
- Reference: `FriendsView` → `selectedProfile` → `ProfileView(viewedProfile:)`.
- Same for Edit Profile → `editProfileDestination` → `WardrobePrivacyView`.

## Don’t

- Nest **`navigationDestination(isPresented:)`** inside a screen that was already presented via `isPresented` (Edit Profile is pushed that way from Profile) — freezes.
- Use classic **`NavigationLink(destination:)`** for these nested profile pushes — also froze Edit Profile → Wardrobe Privacy.
- Wrap Edit Profile / Friends in a second `NavigationStack` unless intentionally isolating like `SettingsView`.
- From a **child**, nil out a **Profile/root-owned** `navigationDestination(item:)` binding in `onAppear` (e.g. `profileReadOnlyItemDestination = nil`). That orphans the parent push; Profile → Item → Outfit → Back can leave a duplicate outfit (or skip item). Keep root-owned bindings until the system pops / clears them.
- On a **nested** other-user `ProfileView`, re-register root destinations (Notifications / Settings / Users / Friends / …). Those fight the active Friends push and can orphan Friends / hide `< Friends`. Nested profiles only attach destinations they need (e.g. Redress).
- Put a custom **`.principal`** toolbar title on other-user Profile — iOS often drops the back-button label (chevron only). Use `.navigationTitle` so `< Friends` can show.

## Nested pushes owned by mid-stack screens

When **Item / Outfit / Pending** owns the next `navigationDestination(item:)` (not Profile), **do** clear that binding on the pushed child’s `onAppear` — otherwise SwiftUI re-evaluates the destination in a loop and freezes. See `navigation-destination-clear-on-appear.mdc`.

## Contrast

| Flow | Method |
|---|---|
| Profile → Edit Profile / Friends / Settings | `navigationDestination(isPresented:)` on Profile root (OK) |
| Friends → other-user profile | `navigationDestination(item:)` (canonical nested push) |
| Edit Profile → Wardrobe Privacy | `navigationDestination(item:)` (match Friends) |
| Settings → child settings | Own inner `NavigationStack` + links (isolated) |
| Item → Outfit / Pending → Edit OutfitAddView | `navigationDestination(item:)` + **clear binding on appear** |
